INT. CLASSROOM - DAY

ZAYAN (9) sits at a wooden desk. He wears a bright red hoodie with a frayed left cuff. His scuffed white trainers tap a rapid rhythm against the floorboards.

He is never still. Tap-tap-tap.

Around his left wrist is a thick red rubber band.

On the teacher's desk sits a glossy book: "THE COSMIC COMMANDER STICKER BOOK". It has a shiny gold cover. Zayan stares at it. He wants it back.

MR. HENDERSON (40s) writes equations on the chalkboard.

MR. HENDERSON
And so, class, the decimal point moves to the left. Just like a train on a single track.

Zayan snaps the rubber band against his wrist. Snap.

ZAYAN
(To himself)
But what if the train has ten tracks? And wings? And a laser booster?

Zayan's eyes dart to the open window. A yellow butterfly flutters. A lawnmower hums outside. A clock ticks. 

He sees it all. He hears it all.

MR. HENDERSON
Zayan! Please focus on the single track.

ZAYAN
Sorry, Mr. Henderson. My brain has too many stations open.

MR. HENDERSON
That sticker book stays on my desk until Monday. No distractions.

Zayan sighs. He looks down at his desk. He rubs the frayed cuff of his hoodie.

EXT. PLAYGROUND - DAY

Kids run across the green grass. 

DEV (9) and PRIYA (9) bounce a blue handball against a brick wall. 

Zayan runs up to them. He bounces on his heels.

ZAYAN
Hey! Can I play? I can do a double-bounce spin-shot!

DEV
We are just playing regular handball, Zayan. You always change the rules.

PRIYA
Yeah. Last time you got distracted by a beetle and the ball hit the principal.

ZAYAN
That beetle had a perfect hexagon on its back! It was a sign!

Priya sighs and catches the ball.

PRIYA
We are going to play with the others. Sorry.

Dev and Priya walk away toward the swings. 

Zayan stands alone. His shoulders drop. He snaps his rubber band. Snap.

ZAYAN
(Whispering)
I have Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder. It is a big name. It just means my brain is a pinball machine. I cannot turn off the extra bumpers.

He looks at the other kids laughing together.

ZAYAN
Sometimes it feels like everyone else has the instruction manual. And mine was printed in a language I do not know. Maybe I am just broken.

INT. HALLWAY - DAY

Zayan, Dev, and Priya walk back inside. The school is quiet.

Along the walls are bright orange and blue panels. Metal tracks line the ceiling and the floor.

MR. HENDERSON
Be careful of the walls, children. The school board is testing the new Modular Space Saver system today.

DEV
What does it do?

MR. HENDERSON
It slides the walls to make new classrooms. Very modern. Very efficient.

Suddenly, a deep mechanical sound rumbles through the floor.

CLACK.

The metal tracks glow blue. 

Zayan stops. His ears perk up.

ZAYAN
That is not a normal click. That is a gears-jamming click.

MR. HENDERSON
I am sure it is just a calibration cycle.

CLACK-CLACK-WHIRR!

A blue wall on the left suddenly slides forward. It blocks the exit to the playground.

An orange wall on the right slides left. It blocks the path to the cafeteria.

PRIYA
Hey! The hallway is shrinking!

MR. HENDERSON
Stay calm! Let me call the main office.

Mr. Henderson reaches for the wall phone. 

CLACK!

A solid steel partition slides down from the ceiling. It lands right between Mr. Henderson and the kids.

MR. HENDERSON
(Muffled behind the wall)
Children! Stay where you are! I will go around!

DEV
Go around where? There is no around left!

They are trapped in a small, square room made of three blue walls and one orange wall.

INT. SHIFTING MAZE - DAY

Dev grips his backpack straps. Priya looks up at the ceiling.

PRIYA
We are trapped! The walls are moving!

Zayan does not panic. His eyes dart from the floor tracks to the ceiling. 

He sees a pattern of flashing lights. Red, blue, blue, orange.

ZAYAN
They are not just moving. They are shuffling. Like a giant deck of cards.

DEV
We are going to get squished!

ZAYAN
No. Look at the tracks. The grooves have safety stops. But they only open for a few seconds.

CLACK!

The blue wall in front of them slides away. It reveals a long corridor. At the end of the corridor is the main lobby.

In the lobby, the trophy cabinet shines. Inside is Zayan's Cosmic Commander sticker book.

ZAYAN
There is my book! And the front doors!

PRIYA
Forget the book, Zayan! We need to get out!

ZAYAN
We can do both. But we have to move. Fast.

DEV
Which way? The walls are moving again!

An orange wall slides across the corridor, blocking the lobby again.

Zayan snaps his rubber band. Snap.

He closes his eyes for one second. The sounds of the gears echo in his mind. 

To a regular brain, it is noise. To Zayan's brain, it is music. 

He hears the low hum of the blue walls. He hears the high whistle of the orange walls. He sees the grid in his mind.

ZAYAN
The blue walls move every thirty seconds. The orange walls move every fifteen seconds. 

DEV
How do you know that?

ZAYAN
My brain tracks everything at once! Usually it is annoying. Right now, it is our map!

PRIYA
Are you sure, Zayan?

ZAYAN
Trust the pinball machine. On my mark! Three! Two! One! Run!

Zayan darts forward. Dev and Priya follow him.

They sprint down the blue corridor.

CLACK!

An orange wall slides right behind them, cutting off the path they just left.

ZAYAN
Don't stop! Left turn! Now!

They slide around a corner. 

A blue wall is sliding closed in front of them. The gap is narrowing.

DEV
It is closing! We cannot make it!

ZAYAN
Yes we can! Slide like you are stealing home base!

Zayan drops to his knees. He slides under the closing blue wall. 

Priya slides right behind him.

Dev hesitates.

ZAYAN
Now, Dev! Jump!

Dev leaps through the gap. He lands on the floor. 

WHAM!

The blue wall slams shut. They are safe on the other side.

Dev pants, looking at Zayan in awe.

DEV
How did you calculate that timing?

ZAYAN
I didn't calculate it. I felt it. The hum changes pitch right before it slides.

PRIYA
You are amazing, Zayan!

Zayan blushes. He rubs his neck. He feels a warm rush in his chest.

ZAYAN
Let's keep going. The main lobby is just past the next orange wall.

INT. TROPHY LOBBY - DAY

They emerge into the wide lobby. The double glass doors to the outside world are fifty feet away.

But the Modular system is in full override.

Three giant walls—one red, one blue, one orange—are sliding back and forth like pistons.

CLACK. WHIRR. CLACK.

The exit is open for only two seconds at a time.

And next to the sliding red wall is the trophy cabinet. The gold cover of the Cosmic Commander sticker book gleams.

DEV
There is the exit! We have to run when they all open at once!

PRIYA
They are moving too fast. We will never time it.

Zayan watches the three walls. He taps his foot. Tap-tap-tap.

His brain sees the paths. 

Path A: Run straight. Get hit by the red wall.

Path B: Wait. The doors lock forever in one minute.

Path C: The Zayan Path.

ZAYAN
The red wall slides left. The blue wall slides right. They cross in the middle. 

PRIYA
So we can't go through the middle!

ZAYAN
No. We use the red wall. It has a ledge on the bottom. We grab the ledge, slide with the wall, grab the book, and land right at the exit.

DEV
That is crazy!

ZAYAN
It is perfect! But we only have thirty seconds before the system locks down.

Zayan snaps his rubber band. Snap.

ZAYAN
Follow me. Do exactly what I do.

Zayan runs toward the sliding red wall.

DEV
Zayan! Wait!

Zayan does not wait. He leaps. 

He grabs the metal ledge on the bottom of the sliding red wall.

He rides the wall as it sweeps across the lobby.

He reaches out his left hand. His frayed cuff catches on the trophy cabinet handle.

He pulls the cabinet door open.

He grabs the Cosmic Commander sticker book!

ZAYAN
Got it!

The red wall is about to crash into the side barrier.

Zayan lets go. He drops to the floor and rolls.

He lands right in front of the double glass doors.

He holds the door open with his foot.

ZAYAN
Dev! Priya! Jump on the blue wall now! It is coming your way!

Dev and Priya look at each other. They run and leap onto the blue wall's ledge.

The blue wall carries them across the lobby, straight toward the door.

ZAYAN
Let go! Now!

They let go. They tumble through the open double doors, landing on the soft green grass outside.

Zayan leaps out behind them.

Behind them, the school doors slam shut with a loud mechanical lock.

CLACK.

The shifting maze is locked. They are safe.

EXT. SCHOOL YARD - DAY

Zayan, Dev, and Priya lie on the grass, panting.

Mr. Henderson runs around the side of the building, breathless.

MR. HENDERSON
Children! You made it out! How did you navigate the shifting corridor algorithm?

Dev points at Zayan.

DEV
Zayan did it. He saw the pattern.

PRIYA
He has a superpower. He can see every possibility at once.

Zayan looks at his Cosmic Commander sticker book. He smiles. 

He stands up and starts bouncing again. He snaps his rubber band. Snap.

ZAYAN
It is not a superpower. It is just Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder. It makes school hard sometimes. But today, it was exactly what we needed.

Dev stands up and brushes off his jeans.

DEV
Hey, Zayan. Do you want to show us that double-bounce spin-shot now?

Zayan's eyes light up.

ZAYAN
Yes! And then I can show you my star stickers! They glow in the dark!

PRIYA
Awesome. Let's play.

They run across the grass together. 

Zayan is still mid-motion. Still bouncing. Still himself. 

And he is exactly where he belongs.

FADE OUT.